2.1 Security Group Scope

Active Directory security groups can have different scopes.

Global

Often used to group users or computers with similar roles or responsibilities.

Domain Local

Often used for assigning permissions to resources within a domain.

Universal

Can be used across multiple domains within an Active Directory forest.

Basic awareness
Global
↓
Group similar accounts

Domain Local
↓
Assign resource permissions

Universal
↓
Cross-domain use
